  "description": "OFURUE crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C146 H119 Dy5 N4 O25,5(C7 H8),0.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.581-5.112 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.22-158.68°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy5(OH)5(Ph2Gly)4(Ph2acac)6]·5C7H8·0.5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 5 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
